window.docContents[204].resolve({"/2___-Basic-notions-of-representation-theory/2___9___-Lie-algebras/Linear-algebraic-groups___-Lie-groups___-and-Lie___s-correspondence/#Chapter2___Discussion_2___9_Lie_groups":{"contents":"The most important examples of Lie groups are linear algebraic groups, which are subgroups of GL_n(\\mathbb{R}) defined by algebraic equations (such as, for example, the group of orthogonal matrices O_n(\\mathbb{R})).\n\nAlso, given a Lie subalgebra \\mathfrak{g} \\subset \\mathfrak{gl}_n(\\mathbb{R}) (which, by Ado's theorem, can be any finite dimensional real Lie algebra), we can define G to be the subgroup of GL_n(\\mathbb{R}) generated by the elements e^X, X \\in \\mathfrak{g}. One can show that this group has a natural structure of a connected Lie group, whose Lie algebra is \\mathfrak{g} (even though it is not always a closed subgroup). While this group is not always simply connected, its universal covering \\widetilde{G} is, and it is the Lie group corresponding to \\mathfrak{g} under Lie's correspondence.\n\nFor more on Lie groups and their relation to Lie algebras, the reader is referred to textbooks on this subject, e.g. [Ki].\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t2. Basic notions of representation theory\t2.9. Lie algebras\tLinear algebraic groups, Lie groups, and Lie's correspondence","header":"Linear algebraic groups, Lie groups, and Lie's correspondence","id":"/2___-Basic-notions-of-representation-theory/2___9___-Lie-algebras/Linear-algebraic-groups___-Lie-groups___-and-Lie___s-correspondence/#Chapter2___Discussion_2___9_Lie_groups"},"/4___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Basic-results/4___4___-Duals-and-tensor-products-of-representations/#chapter-04___section-4-4":{"contents":"\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t4. Representations of finite groups: Basic results","header":"4.4. Duals and tensor products of representations","id":"/4___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Basic-results/4___4___-Duals-and-tensor-products-of-representations/#chapter-04___section-4-4"}});
